    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin adds VSCO Workspace integration to Gravity Forms on your wordpress<br />\ninstallation. This allows you to create forms that will transmit that form data<br />\nto VSCO Workspace and creating a new lead.</p>\n<p>For complete help details see the <a href=\"https://help.workspace.vsco.co/en/articles/640287-using-gravity-forms\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support Site</a></p>\n",
        "installation": "<p>Install <a href=\"http://www.gravityforms.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Gravity Forms</a>.</p>\n<p>Install this plugin. Add your VSCO Workspace <code>Secret Key</code> and<br />\nVSCO Workspace <code>Alias</code> info to the settings page which can be found in<br />\n<a href=\"https://workspace.vsco.co/settings/api/new-lead\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Settings &gt; API Integrations &gt; Legacy New Lead API</a><br />\nsection of VSCO Workspace.  Once a Gravity Form is created, you can go to the settings section<br />\nof the form and map the form fields to the VSCO Workspace fields.</p>\n<p>The most common fields are below:<br />\n  * FirstName<br />\n  * LastName<br />\n  * Email<br />\n  * HomePhone<br />\n  * MobilePhone<br />\n  * WorkPhone<br />\n  * Source<br />\n  * EventDate<br />\n  * JobType<br />\n  * Message</p>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://help.workspace.vsco.co/en/articles/640287-using-gravity-forms\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support Site</a> for a more detailed explanation.</p>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>2.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated for VSCO Workspace.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.13</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Update to setting fields endpoint URL.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.12</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.8</li>\n<li>Updated endpoint URL.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.11</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.10</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.8</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.9</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated settings form to display link correctly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.8</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.7</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.6</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.5</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.3</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 5.2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added Brand field mapping.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Custom fields can now be mapped to dropdown and radio Gravity Form fields.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added the ability for JobRole, JobType, Source to use drop downs for field mappings.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial official release by Táve.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Integrate Gravity Forms with VSCO Workspace",
    "description": "<p>This plugin adds VSCO Workspace integration to Gravity Forms on your wordpress<br />\ninstallation. This allows you to create forms that will transmit that form data<br />\nto VSCO Workspace and creating a new lead.</p>\n<p>For complete help details see the <a href=\"https://help.workspace.vsco.co/en/articles/640287-using-gravity-forms\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support Site</a></p>\n",
